var UcMam=class{constructor(){this.Pm=Ucpd.eCb;this.FU="Generates or edits diagrams including flowcharts, architecture diagrams, ERDs, and more.";this.Lz=1;this.description=["Generates or edits a diagram based on the user's request.\n\n## Capabilities\n- This tool can edit or manipulate shapes in a diagram.\n- This tool should be called when an update or change to a diagram needs to be made.\n  - Prefer this over EditText if the user is trying to incorporate new info into a diagram\n- This tool can handle flowcharts, architecture diagrams, class diagrams, ERD, sequence diagrams, BPMN diagrams and mindmaps.\n- This tool supports creating content with AWS, GCP, Azure, Oracle Cloud, Networking, and Kubernetes shape libraries.\n- This tool has the ability to change the orientation of a diagram, e.g., horizontal vs vertical.\n  - Strongly prefer horizontal diagrams unless the user explicitly asks for vertical\n\n## When to Use This Tool",()=>
UcLam(this)?"- Use this tool when creating NEW diagrams from scratch, **UNLESS** the request is about a business-specific process, organizational workflow, or SOP that is specific to the user's business (not general public knowledge). If it is such a process, you MUST use the switch_agent tool to route it to the Process Agent. **Do NOT route** well-known public or civic processes (e.g., 'how a bill becomes a law', 'the water cycle') — these are general knowledge, not business-specific workflows, and should be handled directly.":
"- Use this tool when creating NEW diagrams from scratch",'- Use this tool when EDITING or ADDING TO existing diagrams (flowcharts, mindmaps, ERDs, etc.)\n  - **IMPORTANT:** Even if the user says "add ideas", "brainstorm", or similar words, if they\'re referring to an EXISTING DIAGRAM, use THIS tool\n  - For example: "add ideas to my mindmap" or "brainstorm more nodes for this flowchart" means EDIT THE DIAGRAM, so use this tool\n- The user will often ask to edit an existing diagram in some way. There are tools that can do simple text replacement, but when the user is asking for part of an existing diagram to have more detail or be removed or be reconnected in some way use this tool.\n- It is better to call this tool for editing a diagram than to call the EditText or AddBlock tools when there is ambiguity.',
()=>UcLam(this)?"- If the user asks to map out, diagram, or document a business process, operational workflow, or SOP that is specific to their business (not general public knowledge) — whether they type the details in chat, attach a document, or ask to start from scratch — DO NOT use this tool. You must invoke switch_agent to hand the request to the Process Agent. **Exception:** Well-known public or civic processes (e.g., 'how a bill becomes a law', 'the water cycle') are general knowledge, not business-specific, and should be handled directly with this tool.":
"- This tool will be able to see the **entire conversation history**. In particular it will be able to see files the user has attached. If the user is asking to generate a diagram from an attached document, this is probably the right tool to call.","## Clarifying Questions\n- If this tool decides it does not have enough information to generate a diagram, it will respond with a *clarifying question* instead of generating a diagram.\n- Look at the `wasDiagramGenerated` field on the result for this tool to tell if it generated a diagram or asked a clarifying question.\n- If `wasDiagramGenerated` is `false` then no diagram was generated, and instead this tool asked a clarifying question.\n- If a clarifying question was asked, the user should be informed that a diagram was not generated and the clarifying question should be displayed to the user.\n\n**IMPORTANT:** If the tool call to generate the diagram is already part of the chat history, DO NOT create a new call for it. Creating a duplicate call will be redundant and unnecessary."];
