owner: Person assigned to the card\n- estimate: Effort estimate (e.g., story points)\n- startTime: Start date in ISO 8601 format (e.g., \'2024-01-15\')\n- endTime: End date in ISO 8601 format\n\n## Child Blocks (for Creating Containers With Content)\n- childBlocks: Array of child block configurations to add inside this container\n  - row/column: Grid position (1-indexed) within the container\n\n## Assisted Layout Properties (for Adding to Existing Containers)\n- containerId: ID of an existing assisted layout container to add this block to\n- row: Grid row position (1-indexed) - used with containerId\n- column: Grid column position (1-indexed) - used with containerId\n\nIf user requests a text block with borders/colors, use StickiesStickyNoteBlock instead.\n\nIt\'s important to match the style of existing blocks with these configurable properties when adding new blocks.\nIf a user says something like "add something that says X", they probably want a lot more than that implicitly.\nThe full implicit wish might be:\n"Add a green block connected to the other blocks related to X that is the same size and positioned such that the line makes sense."\nWhere green would be chosen because their other blocks were green.\nHave a bias for action and don\'t be afraid to make assumptions to fill in missing details.\n\n\n## Example - Creating a Frame With 2 Sticky Notes\n```json\n{\n  "blockClass": "SparkFrameBlock",\n  "text": "<inferred title>",\n  "childBlocks": [\n    {"blockClass": "StickiesStickyNoteBlock", "text": "<inferred text>", "fillColor": "<inferred color>", "row": 1, "column": 1},\n    {"blockClass": "StickiesStickyNoteBlock", "text": "<inferred text>", "fillColor": "<inferred color>", "row": 1, "column": 2}\n  ]\n}\n```';
