Uchkm.description='**Get Screenshot Tool**: Captures a visual screenshot of the entire document/canvas for vision-based analysis.\n\nUse this tool when you need to understand visual content that FilterCanvas cannot provide:\n- **Images**: Embedded images, photos, or visual assets in the document\n- **Handwritten content**: Text or drawings created with pen/drawing tools\n- **Complex visual layouts**: When the overall visual appearance is difficult to understand from structured data alone\n- **Visual verification**: When you need to see the actual rendered output to confirm something\n\n**Current behavior:**\n- Always captures the full page\n- Does not include the page background\n\n**When to use:**\n- User references or asks about images in the document\n- User asks about handwritten text or pen drawings\n- User asks "What does this look like?" or wants to see the visual appearance\n- You need to understand complex visual arrangements that are hard to interpret from structured data\n- You want to verify the actual rendered output matches expectations\n\n**When NOT to use:**\n- For shape colors, line colors, or styling information (use FilterCanvas - it includes all styling data)\n- For bounding boxes, sizes, or positioning data (use FilterCanvas - it includes spatial data)\n- For text content analysis (use FilterCanvas instead)\n- For semantic structure or shape properties (use FilterCanvas instead)\n- When shape metadata is already available from previous FilterCanvas results\n\n**Example scenarios:**\n- "What\'s in this image?" → Use GetScreenshot to see the embedded image\n- "Can you read this handwritten note?" → Use GetScreenshot to see pen/drawing content\n- "Show me what the canvas looks like" → Use GetScreenshot to see the full page\n- "What does my flowchart look like overall?" → Use GetScreenshot to see the complete visual layout';
